Hollywood mourns the loss of Playboy  founder Hugh Hefner et can confirm the  iconic magazine publisher died on  Wednesday at home at the Playboy Mansion  he was 91 years old now family members  and celebrities are paying their  respects Hefner's 26 year old son Cooper  released a statement saying in part  quote my father lived an exceptional and  impactful life as a media and cultural  pioneer and a leading voice behind some  of the most significant social and  cultural movements of our time in  advocating free speech civil rights and  sexual freedom Kendra Wilkinson who  dated Hefner and appeared with him on  their reality series The Girls Next Door  told et quote have changed my life he  made me the person I am today I couldn't  be more thankful for our friendship and  our time together I will miss him so  much but he will be in my heart forever  Kim Kardashian who posed for the mag in  2007 tweeted her condolences so did  Paris Hilton along with some throwback  photos Jenny McCarthy former Playmate of  the Year in 1994 also tweeted about the  mogul thanking him for being a  revolutionary and changing so many  people's lives especially mine singer  The Weeknd tweeted rest in peace while  Rob Lowe called Hefner's death the end  of an era and Ryan Seacrest said he will  forever be remembered as the Hollywood  legend who lived life to the fullest
 

